<h2>Acrylic for TV Units &amp; Living Room Furniture</h2>
<p>The TV wall is the focal point of the living room — and acrylic used selectively here, rather than as an all-over finish, delivers the most impact per rupee of any acrylic application in the home.</p>
<p>The most effective living room acrylic application is as a <strong>accent panel behind the TV</strong> — a single large-format acrylic panel in a statement colour (deep charcoal, burgundy, or a dark natural tone) that frames the screen and creates a high-contrast, photography-ready focal wall. Because this panel is never touched in daily use, high-gloss works perfectly here without any of the fingerprint concerns that plague kitchen applications.</p>
<p>For the <strong>storage cabinets below the TV</strong> or flanking the wall unit, matte acrylic is the recommended choice — these surfaces are opened and touched regularly and will show fingerprints readily in gloss. A dual-tone approach with gloss for the back panel and matte for the cabinet shutters is the 2026 design default for premium Indian living rooms.</p>
