<h2>Acrylic vs Laminate: Which Is Better?</h2>
<p>This is the single most common comparison homeowners research before a kitchen or wardrobe project — and the honest answer depends heavily on which specific room and usage pattern you're designing for.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Criteria</th><th>🟦 Acrylic</th><th>⬜ Laminate</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Appearance</td><td>Deeper colour, glass-like depth WINNER</td><td>Flatter, more printed appearance</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cost (per sq ft)</td><td>₹1,400–₹2,800 installed</td><td>₹400–₹900 installed WINNER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Durability</td><td>Excellent surface, harder to repair if damaged</td><td>Excellent surface, easier to source matching replacement WINNER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>Gloss shows fingerprints; matte is low maintenance</td><td>Generally low maintenance across all finishes WINNER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Lifespan</td><td>15–20 years with care WINNER</td><td>10–15 years typical</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Design Variety</td><td>Mostly solid colours, limited patterns</td><td>Thousands of patterns including wood, stone, textile looks WINNER</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3>Which One Should You Choose?</h3>
<p>Choose <strong>acrylic</strong> for high-visibility, low-contact statement surfaces — kitchen island fronts, TV unit panels, accent wardrobe walls — where the budget allows and visual impact is the priority. Choose <strong>laminate</strong> for larger area coverage, budget-constrained projects, and anywhere pattern variety (wood-look, stone-look) matters more than colour depth.</p>
