</ul></div>
<div class="callout"><span class="callout__title">Note</span><h4>⚠ Consider Alternatives When</h4>
<ul>
  <li>You need heavily profiled or curved door designs → PU Finish</li>
  <li>Pattern variety (wood-look, stone-look) is the priority → Laminate</li>
  <li>Budget is tight across a large project → Acrylic Laminate or Laminate</li>
  <li>Maximum colour customisation matters → PU Spray Finish</li>
  <li>You are specifying for a rental property → Laminate</li>
  <li>Children will use surfaces heavily every day → Matte Laminate</li>
</ul></div></div></div></div>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span><strong>The Single Best Acrylic Decision for 2026</strong><p>Matte acrylic on HDHMR core with PUR edge banding for all high-contact kitchen and wardrobe surfaces — reserving high-gloss acrylic only for low-contact statement surfaces like island fronts, TV back panels, or wardrobe feature walls. This specification delivers the premium acrylic aesthetic without the daily fingerprint and maintenance frustration that gives acrylic a bad reputation in poorly-specified installations.</div>
